%% Fact Book section for Topic 1 — included by content/FB/main.gsm under a "Topic 1" H1.

## T1 · Dates and milestones

::: table | Topic 1 timeline.
@widths 1.6,12.4
@font 9.5
Year | Event
4th c. BCE | Aristotle describes the female as an "incomplete" male — classic essentialism
1792 | Mary Wollstonecraft, *A Vindication of the Rights of Woman*
1869 | J. S. Mill, *The Subjection of Women* — women's "nature" is "an eminently artificial thing"
1871 | Criminal Tribes Act (British India) labels "eunuchs" a criminal class
1935 | Margaret Mead, *Sex and Temperament in Three Primitive Societies*
1949 | Simone de Beauvoir, *The Second Sex*
1955 | John Money coins "gender role"
1966 | Berger and Luckmann, *The Social Construction of Reality*; Kohlberg's cognitive theory; Mischel's social-learning view
1966 | David Reimer injured (raised as a girl on Money's advice; reverted to male in adolescence; died 2004)
1967 | Garfinkel's "Agnes" study; Derrida, *Of Grammatology*
1968 | Robert Stoller, *Sex and Gender*
1969 | First Women's Studies course at Cornell
1970 | First Women's Studies programme, San Diego State College
1972 | Ann Oakley, *Sex, Gender and Society*
1974 | Oakley, *The Sociology of Housework*; Ortner, "Is Female to Male as Nature Is to Culture?"; Rosaldo on the domestic sphere; Bem Sex-Role Inventory; India's *Towards Equality*
1975 | Gayle Rubin, "The Traffic in Women" (sex/gender system); Lakoff, *Language and Woman's Place*; Schulz on semantic derogation; Zimmerman and West on interruptions; Mulvey's "male gaze"; Shirkat Gah founded
1976 | Foucault, *The History of Sexuality*, vol. 1; Condry and Condry "Baby X" study
1977 | US National Women's Studies Association
1978 | Chodorow, *The Reproduction of Mothering*; Kessler and McKenna, *Gender: An Ethnomethodological Approach*
1979 | Goffman, *Gender Advertisements*; MacKinnon, *Sexual Harassment of Working Women*
1980 | Dale Spender, *Man Made Language*
1981 | Bem's gender schema theory; Women's Action Forum founded
1982 | Carol Gilligan, *In a Different Voice*
1983 | Bowles and Klein, *Theories of Women's Studies* — the autonomy/integration debate
1986 | Joan Scott, "Gender: A Useful Category of Historical Analysis"; Lerner, *The Creation of Patriarchy*; Harding, *The Science Question in Feminism*; Aurat Foundation founded
1987 | Connell, *Gender and Power*; West and Zimmerman, "Doing Gender"; Mumtaz and Shaheed, *Women of Pakistan*
1988 | Waring, *If Women Counted*; Pateman, *The Sexual Contract*
1989 | Women's Studies centres at five Pakistani universities
1990 | Butler, *Gender Trouble*; Sedgwick, *Epistemology of the Closet*; Laqueur, *Making Sex*; Tannen, *You Just Don't Understand*; Queer Nation
1990–91 | Teresa de Lauretis coins "queer theory"
1991 | Modleski, *Feminism Without Women*
1993 | Fausto-Sterling, "The Five Sexes"
1994 | Lorber, *Paradoxes of Gender*
1995 | Connell, *Masculinities*
1999 | Nussbaum, "The Professor of Parody"
2000 | Fausto-Sterling, *Sexing the Body*
2002 | Sax's narrow estimate of intersex (≈0.018%)
2004 | Risman: gender as a social structure
2009 | Supreme Court of Pakistan orders recognition of khawaja siras (Aslam Khaki case)
2010 | Cordelia Fine, *Delusions of Gender*
2013 | Alesina, Giuliano and Nunn on the plough and gender roles
2015 | Daphna Joel's "mosaic" brain study
2016 | Gender Studies enters the CSS optional scheme (CE-2016)
2017 | Census counts 10,418 transgender persons
2018 | Transgender Persons (Protection of Rights) Act
2023 | 19 May: Federal Shariat Court holds ss. 2(f), 3 and 7 of the 2018 Act repugnant to Islam
2026 | Appeals before the Shariat Appellate Bench still pending
:::

## T1 · Institutions and publications in Pakistan

::: table
@widths 5,9
Item | Fact
Women's Studies centres (1989) | Quaid-i-Azam University, Islamabad; University of Karachi; University of the Punjab, Lahore; University of Peshawar; University of Balochistan, Quetta — set up by the federal Ministry of Women's Development
Centre of Excellence in Gender Studies (MCQ 2016) | Quaid-i-Azam University
Journals | *Pakistan Journal of Gender Studies* (MCQ 2018); *Pakistan Journal of Women's Studies: Alam-e-Niswan*
Early research bodies | Shirkat Gah (1975); Women's Action Forum (1981); Aurat Foundation (1986)
Policy milestones | National Commission on the Status of Women (2000); National Policy for Development and Empowerment of Women (2002); Gender Reform Action Plan (early 2000s)
CSS | Gender Studies: Group V, code 31, 100 marks, from CE-2016
:::

## T1 · Theories of the social construction of gender

::: table
@widths 3.2,3.8,7
Theory | Thinker(s) and date | Mechanism
Psychoanalytic | Freud; Chodorow (1978) | Identification within the family; mothering reproduces gender
Social learning | Bandura; Mischel (1966) | Reward, punishment, imitation
Cognitive-developmental | Kohlberg (1966) | Identity (2–3), stability (4–5), constancy (6–7)
Gender schema | Bem (1981) | Mental maps filter experience
Interactionist | Goffman (1979); West and Zimmerman (1987) | "Doing gender" in interaction
Performativity | Butler (1990) | Repeated acts create gender
Structural | Lorber (1994); Connell (1987); Risman (2004) | Gender as institution, order and structure
:::

## T1 · Figures and estimates

::: table
@widths 6,8
Figure | Source and note
Intersex births ≈ 0.018% to ≈ 1.7% | Sax (2002) narrow definition; Fausto-Sterling broad definition — always quote as a range
Transgender persons counted: 10,418 | Census 2017 (activists: large undercount)
Female labour-force participation 24.4% | Labour Force Survey 2024–25 (used to show the need for gender analysis)
Female literacy ≈ 53% (male ≈ 68%; overall 60.65%) | Census 2023
Pakistan 143rd of 145 (59.5%) | WEF Global Gender Gap Report 2026 (148th of 148 in 2025)
:::

## T1 · Key quotations

::: table
@widths 8,6
Quotation | Source
"One is not born, but rather becomes, a woman." | Simone de Beauvoir, *The Second Sex* (1949)
"What is now called the nature of women is an eminently artificial thing." | J. S. Mill, *The Subjection of Women* (1869)
"Gender is … a primary way of signifying relationships of power." | Joan Wallach Scott (1986)
"… perhaps it was always already gender …" (of "sex") | Judith Butler, *Gender Trouble* (1990)
"The world historical defeat of the female sex." | Friedrich Engels (1884)
:::
